.TH XYMONAPI 8 "October 29, 2026" "xymon-api"
.SH NAME
xymonapi \- read-only HTTP and JSON interface to the Xymon server
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B "$XYMONHOME/ext/xymonapi/xymonapi.sh"

.SH DESCRIPTION
xymonapi answers HTTP requests with what the Xymon server knows: the status
board, the alarms on it, its hosts, the values in its RRD files and the
graphs drawn from them. Answers are JSON, except for graphs, which are PNG.
It changes nothing in Xymon: it only reads.

It is optional, and shipped disabled. It is started by
.I xymonlaunch(8)
from the task file \fBtasks.d/xymonapi\fR beside tasks.cfg, which its
installation creates with a DISABLED line. To run it, remove that line;
xymonlaunch starts it once xymond is running, and restarts it if it stops.

It needs a Xymon built from its current main branch: its settings go in
xymonserver.d/, which no release of Xymon reads yet. On 4.3.30 a file there
is ignored, password included, and xymonapi then answers anyone.

Unlike the rest of Xymon, xymonapi needs Python 3.10 or later, with the
modules fastapi, uvicorn and yaml (requirements.txt beside it lists them).
When one is missing it logs which, and exits with status 77.

The OpenAPI description of every operation is served at /openapi.json, and
is the file openapi.yaml beside the program.

.SH OPERATIONS
Every path is under /xymon/api/v1. Only GET is accepted, and any other path
answers 404.
.IP "\fB/health\fR"
Whether xymond answers a ping, and the version it reports.
.IP "\fB/states\fR [\fBentity\fR=HOST] [\fBtest\fR=TEST] [\fBverdict\fR=VERDICT]"
The status board, one state per host and test. The colour is given as a
verdict: green is ok, yellow warning, red critical, blue disabled, clear
nodata and purple unknown.
.IP "\fB/alarms\fR"
Every state whose verdict is not ok.
.IP "\fB/entities\fR"
Each host on the board, once.
.IP "\fB/series\fR \fBentity\fR=HOST \fBtest\fR=TEST [\fBmetric\fR=DATASET] [\fBfrom\fR=TIME] [\fBto\fR=TIME]"
The values of one dataset of the RRD file TEST.rrd of HOST, under
$XYMONRRDS, read with rrdtool. DATASET defaults to lambda.
.IP "\fB/graphs\fR \fBentity\fR=HOST \fBtest\fR=TEST [\fBfrom\fR=TIME] [\fBto\fR=TIME]"
The graph
.I showgraph.cgi(1)
draws for HOST and TEST, fetched from $XYMONSERVERCGIURL.
.LP
A TIME is \fBnow\fR, seconds since the epoch, or a time relative to now such
as \fB-30m\fR, \fB-24h\fR, \fB-7d\fR or \fB-2w\fR. \fBfrom\fR defaults to
-24h and \fBto\fR to now. A host or test name that is not one Xymon uses,
or a time it cannot read, is answered with 400.

.SH ENVIRONMENT
The task file loads xymonserver.cfg, and xymonapi uses these settings from it:
.IP "\fBXYMSRV\fR"
The Xymon server to ask. It is required; xymonapi does not fall back to
127.0.0.1.
.IP "\fBXYMON\fR"
The xymon client program.
.IP "\fBXYMONRRDS\fR"
Where the RRD files are, for /series.
.IP "\fBXYMONSERVERCGIURL\fR"
Where showgraph.cgi is, for /graphs.
.LP
Three settings are its own. Put them in a file under
\fBxymonserver.d/\fR beside xymonserver.cfg, which reads its files, for
instance xymonapi.cfg:
.IP "\fBXYMONAPI_LISTEN\fR"
The address and port to listen on, as HOST:PORT or [ADDRESS]:PORT for IPv6.
The default is 127.0.0.1:1986, which only this machine reaches.
.IP "\fBXYMONAPI_PASSWD\fR"
An htpasswd file. When set, every request needs a user and password from it,
and is answered 401 otherwise. It is normally the file the web pages use,
whose users useradm.cgi and chpasswd.cgi manage. The password is checked by
Apache's htpasswd program, which must be on PATH; xymonapi does not start
if it is not, or if it cannot read the file.
When unset, xymonapi answers anyone who can reach it.
.IP "\fBXYMONAPI_PYTHON\fR"
The Python to run the API with, when the modules it needs are not installed
for the system's python3: the python3 of a virtualenv that holds them, for
instance. The default is python3, found on PATH.

.SH FILES
.IP "\fB$XYMONHOME/ext/xymonapi/\fR"
The program: xymonapi.sh, the launcher the task runs; app.py and xymon.py,
the server; openapi.yaml, the description served at /openapi.json; and
requirements.txt, the Python modules it needs.
.IP "\fB$XYMONHOME/etc/tasks.d/xymonapi\fR"
The xymonlaunch task, installed with a DISABLED line. A later installation
leaves it as it is.
.IP "\fB$XYMONHOME/etc/xymonserver.d/\fR"
A file of yours here holds the three settings of its own listed under
ENVIRONMENT. Nothing is installed there.
.IP "\fB$XYMONSERVERLOGS/xymonapi.log\fR"
The log, written through the task's LOGFILE. A missing Python or module is
reported here.
.LP
$XYMONHOME/etc and $XYMONHOME/ext are links to wherever an installation keeps
those directories, /etc/xymon for instance.

.SH NOTES
xymonapi speaks plain HTTP. To reach it from other machines over HTTPS, keep
it on 127.0.0.1 and put a web server in front of it, as for the CGI programs.

It answers one request at a time.

.SH "SEE ALSO"
xymonlaunch(8), tasks.cfg(5), xymonserver.cfg(5), xymon(1), showgraph.cgi(1),
xymon(7)
